  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Dental Assisting A.S. Degree - Local GE' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published August 10, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7628/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: SCC Local AA/AS (the map also notes students may complete Cal-GETC instead of the local pattern). Official Total Units: 60.5-62.5; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 14 + 13 + 16.5 + 15 + 3 = 61.5 units (STAT C1000 at 4 units, first-listed; ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). Semester sums verified against the map's 13-14 / 13-14 / 16.5 / 15 / 3 headers. A Summer Session (DAST 129 Clinical Experience II, 3 units, summer-only) follows Semester 4. Choice slots: (1) STAT C1000 / C1000H / MATH 300, Local Area L2 — STAT C1000 selected (4 units); (2) INDIS 313 / HCD 310, Local Area L7B Life Development Skills — INDIS 313 selected; (3) ENGL C1000 / 488 / ESLW 340, Local Area L1A — ENGL C1000 selected. In-plan prereqs: DAST 119 requires DAST 101, 102, 103, 104, 107; DAST 111, 112, 113, 115, 116 require DAST 101, 102, 103, 104, 107, and 119; DAST 118 requires DAST 111, 112, 113, 115, 116, and 119; DAST 129 requires DAST 111, 112, 113, 115, 116, 118, and 119 — all with grades of 'C' or better. DAST 119 is taken in the same semester as the courses that require it (Semester 4); the validator checks code existence only, and the sequencing is per the official map. Placement prereqs (documented): students not placing directly in STAT C1000 take STAT 10/STAT C1000; students not placing directly in MATH 300 take the MATHS 95/MATH 300 combo (STAT C1000, C1000H, MATH 300 or higher meets eligibility); students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo; ENGL 488 requires ESL 325 with a 'C' or better; ESLW 340 requires ESL 325 or Los Rios assessment placement. AA requirements: 60 degree-applicable units with 2.0 GPA, 12 units within Los Rios, each required course 'C' or better, SCC local GE Areas L1A, L1B, L2, L3, L4, L5, L6, L7A, L7B. Health & Health Profession Meta Majors. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
